      "repair_reason": "- [P1] This PR should wait for contributor-supplied real behavior proof; there is no narrow automated repair lane that can prove the contributor's Windows setup for them.; Cleared: The diff keeps the same trusted System32 taskkill executable path, adds only child-process error handling, and does not change dependencies, CI, secrets, permissions, or command construction. (sha=5cd097227ef8b0049c42b3f4f95a81487441bcee)",
      "review_summary": "The branch adds `error` handlers to the three Windows `taskkill.exe` spawns in `runCommandWithTimeout` so async taskkill start failures fall back to `child.kill(\"SIGKILL\")`.\n\nPR surface: Source +11. Total +11 across 1 file.\n\nReproducibility: yes. for source-level reproduction: current main and the latest release show taskkill child spawns without `error` handlers, and Node documents failed spawns as `error` events rather than successful `spawn` events. No live Windows end-to-end run was performed in this read-only review. ([nodejs.org](https://nodejs.org/api/child_process.html))",
